  "answer": "I've completed the research. Here's a summary of the key findings on OpenAI, Anthropic, and Mistral AI funding in June\u2013July 2026:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**OpenAI \u2014 No new round in the window**\n- Last completed round closed **March 31, 2026**: $122B committed at an **$852B** post-money valuation (co-led by SoftBank; Amazon, Nvidia, Microsoft participating).\n- June\u2013July news was about its **IPO** (confidential S-1 filed June 8, 2026) and a reported **$1 trillion valuation target** that could delay the listing \u2014 not a new private raise.\n\n**Anthropic \u2014 The headline event**\n- **$65B Series H at a $965B post-money valuation** (announced May 28, 2026), overtaking OpenAI as the world's most valuable AI startup. Led by Altimeter, Dragoneer, Greenoaks, and Sequoia.\n- **Confidentially filed for IPO on June 1, 2026**, with a potential listing \"as soon as fall 2026.\"\n- Reported ARR approaching **$50B** by early July.\n\n**Mistral AI \u2014 Imminent/rumored round**\n- **June 12, 2026:** Reported (Bloomberg/TechCrunch) to be in **early-stage talks to raise ~\u20ac3B (~$3.5B) at a ~\u20ac20B (~$23B) valuation** \u2014 but this had **not closed** as of mid-July 2026.\n- Last completed equity round: **Sept 2025 Series C, \u20ac1.7B at \u20ac11.7B**, led by ASML. Plus an **$830M debt round in March 2026**.\n\n**Important caveats:** Mistral's \u20ac3B round was still rumored/unconfirmed, and both OpenAI's and Anthropic's IPOs were pending as of the research date. The full report with all data points and sources has been submitted via the structured output.",
